    "title": "FBI offers $30,000 reward in cold case killing of 10-year-old Arizona girl - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By DAVID IVERSEN ,\n14 hours ago The FBI is offering up to $30,000 for information leading to an arrest and conviction in the 1996 sexual assault and killing of a 10-year-old girl in Yuma. Amberly Mendoza was found dead in the bedroom on March 9, 1996 after Yuma police officers responded to a disturbance call. Investigators determined an unknown person entered the residence, sexually assaulted the child and killed her. Read full article\n1",
